Topics Covered:
1.  Network Security Fundamentals
2.  CIA Triad
  - Confidentiality
  - Integrity
  - Availability
3.  Encryption
4.  Symmetric Encryption
5.  Asymmetric Encryption
6.  AES (Advanced Encryption Standard)
7.  RSA (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman)
8.  Hashing
9.  SHA-256
10. Digital Signatures
11. TLS (Transport Layer Security)
12. HTTPS Security
13. Firewalls
14. VPN (Virtual Private Network)
15. DoS (Denial of Service)
16. DDoS (Distributed Denial of Service)
17. MITM (Man-in-the-Middle)
18. Phishing
19. Spoofing
20. Brute Force Attacks

Key Takeaways:
- Learned the three goals of network security: Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability.
- Understood the difference between encryption and hashing.
- Learned symmetric encryption using a shared secret key.
- Learned asymmetric cryptography using public and private keys.
- Understood AES as a symmetric encryption algorithm.
- Understood RSA as an asymmetric cryptographic algorithm.
- Learned cryptographic hashing and SHA-256.
- Understood the purpose of digital signatures.
- Learned the role of TLS in securing network communication.
- Understood how HTTPS uses TLS to provide secure web communication.
- Learned the basic role of firewalls in controlling network traffic.
- Understood VPNs as secure tunnels over untrusted networks.
- Learned the basic concepts of DoS, DDoS, MITM, phishing, spoofing, and brute-force attacks.
